──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Third-party algorithmic references
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

`kernel/src/query/vector/hnsw_core.rs` — fresh implementation of the
Hierarchical Navigable Small World algorithm.

  - Algorithm originally described in:
        Malkov, Yu. A., and Yashunin, D. A.
        "Efficient and robust approximate nearest neighbor search
        using Hierarchical Navigable Small World graphs."
        arXiv:1603.09320, 2016.

  - Structural patterns (per-layer adjacency representation, the
    entry-point promotion check, the bidirectional-connection
    pruning loop) were cross-checked against:
        hnsw_rs by Jean-Pierre Both (<jeanpierre.both@gmail.com>)
        Dual-licensed Apache-2.0 / MIT.
        https://crates.io/crates/hnsw_rs

    Eigenius does not vendor or redistribute hnsw_rs source code.
    `hnsw_core.rs` is a fresh implementation written against the
    paper, with hnsw_rs used as a reference for naming and
    corner-case interpretation. We acknowledge the prior art under
    the Apache-2.0 attribution requirements.
